  "assumptions": {
    "geometry": "Both halves of the symmetric scalar well translate by X=b sin\u00b2(pi |w|/H). Only one arm is coupled to the longitudinal carrier. H is half the relaxed one-increment length. The other arm contributes tension and wave overlap. A true unilateral displacement would change the wave vertex and is outside this comparison. Fixed uniform radius, fixed intake to first order, no oscillatory dipole feed imposed. The angular integral of the forced current is zero.",
    "wall": "Tension uses exact translated round sections dA=R\u00b2 sqrt(1+(Xprime cos(theta))\u00b2) dw dOmega. Volume and end caps are fixed. K_sigma per arm=(4pi/3) sigma R\u00b2 pi\u00b2/(2H). The more general wall action projects to M=(4pi/3) int mu_eta f\u00b2 dw and K=(4pi/3) int [T_w fprime\u00b2+(K_eta+2T_Omega)f\u00b2]dw over both arms, with densitized coefficients. The side-area calculation realizes one particular stiffness, counted once. Archive calibrates only radius/length collective variables. Examples allocate rho0*V to normal radial motion on the side even if another microscopic partition would be possible. The two positive profiles scale as constant or 0.02+f^4. Their integral is matched. Cap inertia, extra pinning, other dissipative wall material and unknown steady contact stiffness are not added in the spectral examples.",
    "wave": "The occupied scalar monopole with action I and translated potential has Vprime=-f*d_x V, Vsecond=f\u00b2*d_x\u00b2 V. The static curvature is I/(2ws) times <s|Vsecond|s>-2<v|(H1-ws\u00b2)^(-1)|v>, v=Vprime*s. Direct curvature and relaxed curvature are alternatives at different stages of elimination. The reduced diagonal wave-force coefficient at finite frequency begins at Kdirect, and its off-diagonal is Kdirect/2 from coherent pump modulation. Let W(nu)=I/(2ws)<v|(H1-(nu+i0)\u00b2)^(-1)|v>; omit the selected bound dipole only in W_rest(z). The two wall diagonals subtract W_rest(z)+W(z\u00b12ws), and their off-diagonal subtracts W_rest(z). The common central dipole couples to both wall components with g/2. The high scalar satellite has an absorber and the other scalar Green functions are below the bulk continuum. The coherent pump is held fixed, zero bare loss, three central/sideband amplitudes. Higher wall harmonics and nonlinear corrections not assessed.",
    "carrier": "A one-arm GNLS real finite reservoir grounded at large distance gives Pi(0) and the low-omega slope with all other wall harmonics clamped. For A+i omega B, source s+i omega t, real A symmetric, B skew, the induced mass is (t-B A^-1 s)^T A^-1(t-B A^-1 s)/2. Direct low-frequency force checked on each mesh. This is an induced reaction in the finite-box limit taken first. Pi(0) is a static softening; any additional direct steady contact term would require independent calibration. For the spectrum use the full measured complex carrier reaction without separately adding its induced mass. The historical trial uses Ktrial+Pi(0)-Pi(omega), the new examples Ksigma+Kdirect-Pi(omega) with scalar corrections as above. The carrier-only dissipative control zeros only the high scalar ImW; all reactive terms are retained.",
    "readout": "FWHM of the central susceptibility supplies the narrow transition width. Construct two Lorentzians with equal areas, widths 1:3, common shift, and conservative spacing |U|/action. Count the maxima of that signal. The fold value 0.503226486865 is from mouth_carrier_bend_work.json. It is not a bound on arbitrary readouts or microscopic line shapes. Local root in tested mass range; monotonicity sampled at 25 points.",
    "gravity": "This bend vanishes at both endpoints; no calibration of freely translating mouth inertia or Newtonian coupling."
  },
  "review": {
    "scope": "Independent local review and calculations, including finite angular quadrature of the translated well and a separate three-by-three spectral inverse with linear interpolation. The identified coherent off-diagonal and dynamic scalar channels were included in the reported spectrum.",
    "verdict": "Scoped review found no outstanding objection to the corrected three-frequency calculation.",
    "conditions": "The physical wall inertia profile, additional wall restoring terms and experimental readout remain open."
  },
